  "id": "COMPOUND:2041 - PROTEIN:2571",
  "verbalization": "The visible evidence suggests a complex but consistent relationship between K-252a and Aminopeptidase S, mediated through Theasaponin E1. The drug K-252a is shown to have targets in the phosphatidylinositol 4-phosphate 3-kinase C2 domain-containing subunit beta and in the solute carrier organic anion transporter family members 2A1 and 3A1, all of which are targets of Theasaponin E1. Theasaponin E1, in turn, is directly linked to Aminopeptidase S. This suggests that K-252a may act through Theasaponin E1 to modulate Aminopeptidase S, potentially through a mechanism involving the transporters or enzymatic activity of the latter. The evidence is robust, with multiple independent pathways converging on the same target hierarchy, indicating a likely functional relationship. The integration of these pathways highlights the role of Theasaponin E1 as a key mediator in the drug's interaction with Aminopeptidase S, though the exact mechanism of action remains to be fully elucidated.",
